+{"connection_id":"BC-a62dd38d1eb370637115","ref":"WLC:Deut.32.2","status":"accepted","reason":"The Hebrew verse directly compares teaching to rain/dew on tender grass, the Mosaic form of the selected rain-and-word motif.","paragraphs":[69],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.32.2","WLC:Isa.55.10","WLC:Isa.55.11"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e9ee50fed120e9a582c2","ref":"WLC:Deut.32.3","status":"rejected","reason":"Moses proclaims the divine name and greatness, but Psalm 135:1 gives the explicit liturgical summons to praise the name and Malachi 3:16 adds the feared name and written remembrance.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.32.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b1ef737e4b15f508e425","ref":"WLC:Deut.32.46","status":"rejected","reason":"Moses tells Israel to heed and teach Torah words, a valid practice, but the selected Exodus 24:4/7 already joins actual writing with public reading; this adds no independent image in paragraph 73.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.32.46"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-44e273c51ea70fe6f018","ref":"WLC:Deut.32.47","status":"rejected","reason":"Torah words are Israel's life in the land, not the surah's better enduring afterlife; treating the two life claims as identical would erase the verse's land setting.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.32.47"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-37c4826b57a53861f531","ref":"WLC:Deut.4.12","status":"rejected","reason":"Israel hears a voice from Sinai fire without a visible form, a different collective revelation scene; Exodus 3:2–4 supplies Moses' bush call more directly.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.4.12"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ca065189c78c8d181770","ref":"WLC:Deut.4.9","status":"rejected","reason":"Israel is warned not to forget Horeb experiences and to teach children; 87:6 is a promise to the reciter, not this communal command, and paragraph 73 centers Moses' pages.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.4.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d73fca78f02c794f09bd","ref":"WLC:Deut.6.6","status":"rejected","reason":"Words on Israel's heart are a broad memory practice; there is no explicit writing, nonforgetting promise, fire, or field detail to add here.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.6.6"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-42e0b54faf2bd8a8ebe1","ref":"WLC:Deut.6.7","status":"rejected","reason":"Rehearsing Torah to children day and night is distinct from the reciter's promised memory; Exodus 24:7 more directly joins written Mosaic words to public oral reading.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.6.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-fdba9746f28f329f3f46","ref":"WLC:Exod.13.21","status":"accepted","reason":"The Hebrew verse explicitly has God guide Israel's way at night with a pillar of fire, stated in paragraph 68's annotation.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.13.21"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-868b031dee505c6f0c7f","ref":"WLC:Exod.13.21","status":"accepted","reason":"The same fire-for-light and road-guidance combination is an exact textual point, distinct from the bush story.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.13.21"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-092d2b75127af5e818ae","ref":"WLC:Exod.17.14","status":"rejected","reason":"A memorial of the Amalek episode is written and recited to Joshua, but its subject is military erasure, not the bush, surah's admonition, or general Mosaic pages; Exodus 24 is closer.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.17.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-1557791c2cdeb831989d","ref":"WLC:Exod.20.24","status":"rejected","reason":"God promises blessing where he causes his name to be remembered at an altar; it is a worship ordinance distinct from Moses' bush naming, for which Exodus 3:15 is direct.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.20.24"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b60cbf399a2729ded704","ref":"WLC:Exod.24.4","status":"accepted","reason":"Moses writes all the divine words, the first step of the selected writing-and-reading counterpart to 87:19.","paragraphs":[73],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.24.4","WLC:Exod.24.7","WLC:Deut.31.24"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-PRL-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-9631b631be936b824ea3","ref":"WLC:Exod.24.7","status":"accepted","reason":"Moses reads the covenant book in the people's ears, joining written pages to spoken reception as the annotation says.","paragraphs":[73],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.24.4","WLC:Exod.24.7","WLC:Deut.31.24"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-PRL-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e34f17921ccd0b97ca51","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.10","status":"accepted","reason":"God sends Moses from the bush encounter to Pharaoh, the mission dimension of paragraph 68's fire scene.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.2","WLC:Exod.3.4","WLC:Exod.3.10","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-PRL-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-bb4846b67a1f697e060f","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.10","status":"accepted","reason":"The Hebrew sends Moses to Pharaoh and to lead Israel out, tying the fire-side call to the later Egypt opposition.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.2","WLC:Exod.3.4","WLC:Exod.3.10","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-PRL-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c29453efd751b2788402","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.12","status":"accepted","reason":"After Moses' sending, God promises that the people will worship at this mountain; the annotation states the call-to-worship sequence.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.2","WLC:Exod.3.4","WLC:Exod.3.10","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-PRL-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0c83e068065f4549abae","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.12","status":"accepted","reason":"Worship on the mountain is the explicit ritual outcome of the bush commission, kept distinct from the surah's prayer wording.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.2","WLC:Exod.3.4","WLC:Exod.3.10","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-PRL-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-159ca9cbbf6cb883d3d5","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.14","status":"rejected","reason":"The verse reveals God's self-identification to Moses, but does not mention a hidden hour; Exodus 3:15, selected separately, supplies the explicit name/remembrance link.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2492a702fca0dcc23434","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.14","status":"rejected","reason":"God's self-identification is indeed in the bush sequence, but the proposed name and remembrance relation is stated explicitly in the next verse, Exodus 3:15, so 3:14 adds no second point here.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c10782337f6bfaba0e4c","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.15","status":"accepted","reason":"The revealed name is called God's memorial for generations, an explicit Moses-scene name/remembering link.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.15"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-SYD-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a19040f5a61560badd0b","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.15","status":"accepted","reason":"The actual WLC form is zikhri rather than the proposed zēker; it is still from the Hebrew z-k-r remembering root cognate with Arabic dhikr.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.15"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-SYD-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-5bc45b28a3f9cf0cb906","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.15","status":"accepted","reason":"The Hebrew zikhri form and Arabic li-dhikri share the Semitic remembering root in corresponding Moses scenes; the annotation keeps their functions distinct.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.15"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-SYD-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-81b5e3e2d68d99dbae95","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.2","status":"accepted","reason":"Hebrew says the bush burns without being consumed, grounding the selected non-consuming fire encounter.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.2","WLC:Exod.3.4","WLC:Exod.3.10","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-PRL-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-1738e0a5cceef627e4b0","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.2","status":"accepted","reason":"The nonconsumed bush's outcome is contrasted, not equated, with the human destined to enter great fire; the annotation states that limit.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.2","WLC:Exod.3.4","WLC:Exod.3.10","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-PRL-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-fbc724b7acda39c6fd2d","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.3","status":"rejected","reason":"Moses turning aside to inspect the bush is context for the call in 3:4 and not a second independent road-guidance claim; Exodus 13:21 states guiding fire directly.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7905d6574a5376f61334","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.4","status":"accepted","reason":"God calls Moses by name from the bush after he turns aside, the call-and-response element stated in paragraph 68.","paragraphs":[68],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.2","WLC:Exod.3.4","WLC:Exod.3.10","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-PRL-001"]}

