+{"connection_id":"BC-4accca49c36e852ce4f3","ref":"WLC:Ps.1.3","status":"rejected","reason":"The Torah-delighting person is a stream-planted tree whose leaf does not wither, but paragraph 71 turns on worked ground and a chosen future; Hebrews 6 supplies both crop outcomes.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.1.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0e6f452e73fd8be2bdda","ref":"WLC:Ps.1.3","status":"rejected","reason":"It repeats BC-4accca49c36e852ce4f3 at the same verse; the tree's steady fruit is different from the field's rain and chaff/froth sorting.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.1.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-88620b230fec1a1daf7f","ref":"WLC:Ps.1.4","status":"rejected","reason":"The wicked are chaff carried by wind, not the valley flood's foam; the motion and material differ from paragraph 69's specific water image.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.1.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-003be0ee86469437d01c","ref":"WLC:Ps.1.4","status":"rejected","reason":"It repeats BC-88620b230fec1a1daf7f: wind-driven chaff is an agricultural loss image, but neither measured flood nor surviving useful material appears.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.1.4"],"annotations":[]}
