+{"connection_id":"BC-5b15fecfe75a7b857bc9","ref":"WLC:Ps.103.17","status":"rejected","reason":"The enduring term is God's steadfast love toward those who fear him, not explicitly the afterlife or a surviving crop; Isaiah 40 supplies grass plus enduring word more directly.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.103.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-18e4b9717406b00ea768","ref":"WLC:Ps.104.11","status":"rejected","reason":"WLC Psalm 104:11 says field animals drink; the springs through valleys are in 104:10, so this cited verse does not state the proposed valley-stream image.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.104.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7dbd80f2379cc60911b4","ref":"WLC:Ps.104.14","status":"rejected","reason":"God grows grass for beasts and cultivated plants for human food, but the verse lacks the drying/refuse or moral choice that paragraph 71 turns on.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.104.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-965aa6d95ab7855b80b8","ref":"WLC:Ps.104.14","status":"rejected","reason":"It repeats BC-7dbd80f2379cc60911b4's pasture/useful-produce distinction without the subsequent failing-versus-enduring outcome.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.104.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ce53da03d42cca8a0825","ref":"WLC:Ps.119.105","status":"rejected","reason":"God's word is a lamp for feet and light for a path, but the image is figurative; Exodus 13:21 gives the literal fire and road guidance in paragraph 68.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.119.105"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7e89b4cf793529894504","ref":"WLC:Ps.139.14","status":"rejected","reason":"WLC Psalm 139:14 praises wondrous making but says nothing of womb weaving; the womb is 139:13 and the hidden crafting is 139:15, so the cited verse overstates its detail.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.139.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-fa2d29281d259e6f989a","ref":"WLC:Ps.139.15","status":"rejected","reason":"The body is made in secret and embroidered in earth's depths, but neither chosen mission nor cultivated pasture appears; Genesis 2 and Isaiah 44 more fully serve paragraph 72.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.139.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f18e416d22bdf6a6e49c","ref":"WLC:Ps.148.13","status":"accepted","reason":"The psalm calls for praise of the divine name because it alone is exalted, the name/highness side of paragraph 73's selected arc.","paragraphs":[73],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.14.22","WLC:Ps.7.18","WLC:Ps.148.13","WLC:Mal.3.16"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-011"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-8166f1b5dd6beac9dd3a","ref":"WLC:Ps.37.3","status":"rejected","reason":"WLC Psalm 37:3 urges trust and good action; the wicked-withering-like-grass line is 37:2, not the cited verse.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.37.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-aa69248c422b80a98ce4","ref":"WLC:Ps.37.38","status":"rejected","reason":"WLC Psalm 37:38 says the wicked's future is cut off; the peaceful future of the blameless is in 37:37, not the cited verse.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.37.38"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-4448efa0dd8fd9bb2027","ref":"WLC:Ps.65.11","status":"rejected","reason":"God waters furrows and blesses growth, but Isaiah 55:10–11 more directly links productive rain to an effective spoken word, the distinctive step of paragraph 69.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.65.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-478f9154cdb77cbad680","ref":"WLC:Ps.7.18","status":"accepted","reason":"The psalmist sings the name of YHWH Most High, an unusually close praise/name/highness formula in paragraph 73's annotation.","paragraphs":[73],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.14.22","WLC:Ps.7.18","WLC:Ps.148.13","WLC:Mal.3.16"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-011"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-5b7b57ab0bb40b18fba0","ref":"WLC:Ps.7.18","status":"accepted","reason":"Hebrew Elyon and Arabic al-A'la are cognate highness forms; the psalm uses the title while praising the divine name, as the annotation says.","paragraphs":[73],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.14.22","WLC:Ps.7.18","WLC:Ps.148.13","WLC:Mal.3.16"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-MTF-011"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6e6d9aca2af21a548836","ref":"WLC:Ps.90.7","status":"rejected","reason":"WLC Psalm 90:7 speaks of divine anger, not morning/evening grass; that grass sequence is WLC 90:5–6.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.90.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-4922da23b6b443b52277","ref":"WLC:Ps.92.14","status":"rejected","reason":"Righteous people are planted in God's house, but paragraph 71's worked earthly field and afterlife comparison is a different agricultural frame.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.92.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-5a35704a41e9b8812c4c","ref":"WLC:Ps.92.15","status":"rejected","reason":"Fruit in old age expresses longevity of the righteous, not an afterlife harvest or contrast with the world's drying pasture.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.92.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-30b5b3102fe46204ba3c","ref":"WLC:Ps.92.8","status":"rejected","reason":"The wicked sprout like grass only to be destroyed, but the verse does not set a useful cultivated counterpart beside it; Isaiah 40:6–8 gives the stronger drying/enduring contrast.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.92.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ab3e3c188725d229331b","ref":"WLC:Zech.13.9","status":"rejected","reason":"A remnant is refined through fire and calls God's name, but the people pass inside fire for purification; this is neither Moses beside a calling fire nor the doomed person of 87:12–13.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Zech.13.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7ac786b08f93c7bd5bdc","ref":"Wisdom of Solomon 11:20","status":"unavailable","reason":"This Wisdom passage is absent from the frozen local snapshot; its measure/number/weight wording cannot be verified here.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2a0f2dfd09a857dc6294","ref":"Wisdom of Solomon 11:20","status":"unavailable","reason":"The same named Wisdom passage is absent locally; the second measure proposal also remains unverified.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-db871c779ab8bfe2e70a","ref":"Wisdom of Solomon 17:7","status":"unavailable","reason":"This Wisdom passage is absent locally; its account of Egyptian magic cannot be checked.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ed6ff2bdc1925e341d41","ref":"Wisdom of Solomon 3:1","status":"unavailable","reason":"This Wisdom verse is absent locally; the proposed righteous-beyond-torment contrast cannot be verified.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e6d00dbef64b03fd36ef","ref":"Wisdom of Solomon 3:4","status":"unavailable","reason":"This Wisdom verse is absent locally; its immortality wording cannot be checked.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d1bbce55025ee7c602da","ref":"Wisdom of Solomon 7:1","status":"unavailable","reason":"This Wisdom verse is absent locally; its womb-formation detail cannot be checked.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
