+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.1","status":"rejected","reason":"Moses tends the flock and comes to Horeb here, while Exodus 3:2–12 provides the decisive fire, call, and mission details used for paragraph 68.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.1"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.6","status":"rejected","reason":"The divine self-identification and Moses' hidden face add narrative context, but not a separate connection to the paragraph 68 treatment of his call.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.3.6"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"SBLGNT:Matt.13.26","status":"rejected","reason":"The growing weeds and grain relate only broadly to vegetation; the selected Hebrews 6 field contrast more directly fits paragraph 71.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Matt.13.26"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"SBLGNT:Rev.8.7","status":"rejected","reason":"Burned green grass here belongs to a trumpet plague and does not illuminate the paragraph 71 contrast of transient growth with ultimate life.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Rev.8.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.3.12","status":"accepted","reason":"Paul's contrasting durable and combustible building materials begin the fire-test sequence cited in the paragraph 69 Christian comparison.","paragraphs":[69],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.3.12","SBLGNT:1Cor.3.13","SBLGNT:1Cor.3.14","SBLGNT:1Cor.3.15"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"SBLGNT:Heb.6.9","status":"rejected","reason":"The reassurance after the field warning lacks the rain, crop, and thorn imagery that grounds the selected Hebrews 6:7–8 connection.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Heb.6.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"CORPUSCORANICUM:87:18-19:anmerkung","status":"accepted","reason":"The note distinguishes the Qur'anic reference to the earlier scrolls of Abraham and Moses from a direct quotation, a qualification used in the paragraph 73 research annotation.","paragraphs":[73],"evidence":["CORPUSCORANICUM:87:18-19:anmerkung"],"annotations":["S087-TEV-YNT-001"]}
*** End Patch"));

